<!--
  The row control that opens §6's hierarchy menu: a bar with an arrow pushing in under it, and the line the row
  would land on beneath both.

  It is not the card's fold chevron (§7) and not the drag handle (§3): three shapes for three verbs, because a reader
  who mistakes one for another moves their data. The geometry is closed polygons rather than a stroke, so it reads at
  the 36dp the panel's own padding leaves it — the same box `ic_edit` and `ic_delete` are drawn in.
-->
